    "source_scope_note": "The selected problem is the exact original composite Theorems6.5 and6.7: existence by genuine stable convergence of the finite-rank scaled power-sum Macdonald operator, its exact eigenvalues and the resulting simple joint spectrum with stable Cherednik operators over Q(q,t). Complete author Sections1--6 through1361 retain the earlier basis/convergence definitions, alternative finite-idempotent description, all kappa convergence/separation and the entire new operator proof1295--1347 plus joint-spectrum proof1359--1361. The already counted first-main basis result is necessary supporting context, not independently counted again; the remaining new obligation is convergence on arbitrary convergent polynomial sequences, handled by the full authored symmetric-tail/idempotent computation, not merely a diagonal extension on eigenvectors. Author1284 and1351--1353 explicitly distinguish this construction from eigenvector-only convergence and the sum of the stable Cherednik operators. Later arbitrary symmetric-operator conjectures are unselected and remain only exact printed references. The sole fixed augmented numerical filling is an exact original diagram-only asset with absent-cell positions; all surrounding general formulas and human proof remain editable. Exactly five literal mathbbm{1} indicators194/358/639/640/1258 use root-approved pinned Noto U+1D7D9 mathord with proportional text/script math styles, strict1-only whitelist and disclosed stroke/width/placement differences. Literal exponents/function arguments are unchanged; no denied package acquisition or generalized emulation.",
